  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A frictionless wire $\\mathrm{AB}$ is fixed on a sphere of radius $\\mathrm{R}$. A very small spherical ball slips on this wire. The time taken by this ball to slip from A to $\\mathrm{B}$ is\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/r_OrMPvilqMNy6lx1g52JXylmmTCE4Iq5qfXm1-nk1k.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fHX9f",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2 g R}}{g \\cos \\theta}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tYrRo",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{g R} \\cdot \\frac{\\cos \\theta}{g}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "E3BLH",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{\\frac{R}{g}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JakY1",
      "text": "$\\frac{g R}{\\sqrt{g \\cos \\theta}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Acceleration of body along $\\mathrm{AB}$ is g $\\cos \\theta$ Distance travelled in time $\\mathrm{t}$ sec $=$\r\n\r\n$A B=\\frac{1}{2}(g \\cos \\theta) t^{2}$\r\n\r\nFrom $\\Delta \\mathrm{ABC}, \\mathrm{AB}=2 \\mathrm{R} \\cos \\theta$\r\n\r\nThus, $2 \\mathrm{R} \\cos \\theta=\\frac{1}{2} g \\cos \\theta t^{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow t^{2}=\\frac{4 R}{g} \\Rightarrow t=2 \\sqrt{\\frac{R}{g}}$",
    "image": null
  },
